    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535-a3">

                <pb facs="0946" n="850" xml:id="pg850"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 3—Translation]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Panaman Commissioners to the American
                        Commissioners</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-07-28"><hi rendition="#italic">July 28,
                        1926</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: The Panaman Commissioners have received
                    with great gratification the note of this date in which the American
                    Commissioners confirm the understanding arrived at in the present negotiations
                    with regard to the statue of Columbus now standing in the grounds of the
                    Washington Hotel in the city of Colon, presented to the Republic of Colombia in
                    1866 by Eugenie, Empress of the French, and the ownership of which is recognized
                    to correspond to the Republic of Panama, with the right to remove it to such
                    place within the territory of the Republic, as may be convenient.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. J. Alfaro</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eusebio A. Morales</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
